1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,800
A transaction list shows what I spent.
It does not make me want to review it.

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:13,000
The Listening Ledger turns that review
into a book I can open and explore.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Each purchase has a short sound.
Green means within the applicable limits.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Red needs attention. Blue means
there is still something to check.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
[Warm chord — within limits]

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,000
[Wooden taps — needs attention]

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,000
[Glass tones — needs review]

8
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Now I switch to PayPal Sandbox.
This authorized test account contains a twelve-dollar purchase.

9
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:47,000
The importer preserves its amount, currency and source,
while excluding non-purchase events. No real money moves.

10
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:53,500
This purchase was a virtual study notebook
used for testing. I supplied that context.

11
00:00:53,500 --> 00:01:01,000
Here is the saved review from an actual DeepSeek request,
with the original input still visible.

12
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:08,000
The model suggested Education and quoted
the words supporting that suggestion.

13
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:12,500
It did not decide whether
I recognized the purchase.

14
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:18,000
I accepted the category, then separately confirmed
that I knew this transaction.

15
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:23,500
These are two recorded human decisions.
The original twelve-dollar amount stays unchanged.

16
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:30,000
The journal keeps the source information and my review
separately, so I can revisit both.

17
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:35,000
[Device voice · voice-setting sample]
Pinecone Coffee: eighteen yuan.

18
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:39,500
This did not trigger
your overspending alert.

19
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:45,000
Another purchase is twenty-six dollars and fifty cents.
Its category still needs review.

20
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:51,000
My budget is a rule I set,
not a judgment from AI.

21
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:58,500
Changing the monthly limit from twenty-five dollars
to ten previews an alert.

22
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:04,000
I cancel the change.
The original budget remains.

23
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:11,500
I can also open the Spending Collection.
It groups the same records by category, with a different page design.

24
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:18,000
The purchase and my saved decision
remain the same.

25
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Reopening restores the review.
Repeat synchronization and restart recovery were also verified.

26
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:31,000
This is a working local prototype,
tested with one controlled Sandbox account.

27
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:36,000
Listen for a signal. Inspect the evidence.
Make the decision yourself.

28
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:40,000
The Listening Ledger:
a spending review you can hear and revisit.
